Get coins with the latest market data with different filters and sorting options
GET
https://public-api.dropstab.com/api/v1/coins
This method allows you to request various data about coins using different filters and sorting options. trading variable represents the different trading statuses that a coin can have. Below are the descriptions of each status:
•	CURRENTLY_TRADING
Represents coins or tokens that are currently being actively traded on exchanges.
•	NOT_YET_TRADING
Represents coins or tokens that are planned to be traded but have not yet started trading (ICOs, IDOs, Possible airdrops, etc.).
•	NO_LONGER_TRADING
Represents coins or tokens that were traded in the past but are no longer active in trading on exchanges.
•	ALL
Represents all possible statuses, including currently trading, not yet trading, and no longer trading.
Example usage:
You can retrieve different sets of coins by applying filters and sorting. For example, to get the top gainers from the top 300 ranked coins, you should specify the following parameters:
•	sortOrder: DESC (sort in descending order)
•	sortingField: PRICE_CHANGE_24H (field to sort by — price change in the last 24 hours)
•	rankFrom: 1 (rank from 1)
•	rankTo: 300 (rank to 300)
This request will return a list of coins sorted by the highest price increase over the last 24 hours within the specified rank range.
